    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: default `registrationDate` to the server's current date\n\nWhen no registration date is supplied on owner creation, it's set to today; the field is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format. A supplied date is preserved.\n\n### Files touched\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto` and (via `allOf`) `OwnerDto` with a `LocalDate registrationDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`. MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions, so no mapper edits were needed.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. (`ddl-auto=none`, so the schema comes from these scripts; tests run on hsqldb.)\n\n4. **`DefaultRegistrationDate.java`** (new function) \u2014 a single-responsibility step that sets `LocalDate.now()` only when the built owner's registration date is null, mutating the owner in place per the `@Val` convention.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline between `build` and `save`, under the same transaction governance.\n\nThe default logic lives in its own small function rather than being folded into `BuildOwner`, keeping each step focused. Both new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full suite pass.",
